    "title": "Base of a medieval Easter candlestick",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10325786",
    "publication_date": "2017-06-22",
    "description": "The two Lions are the base of a spiral  Easter candlestick.   The inscription: CRUDELES OPE indicates the author of the work. The date of the completion of the candelabrum  is on the rights side: AD MCCXLV MEN(SIS) OCT (OBRIS) DIE ULTIMA. The work is to be attributed to a cosmatesque School and is situated in the cathedral of Terracina, ITaly\n\nSource: Objaverse 1.0 / Sketchfab",
